    "redesign": {
      "utc_date": "2026-10-25",
      "reason": "LeWM TwoRoom's goal cost (latent distance to the goal frame) is informative only within about 30 px of the target and flat or non-monotone beyond (rank correlation 0.41 with true distance over the arena), while its predictor is accurate (block squared error 14 to 36 against a displacement scale of 384). The paper evaluates TwoRoom with goals 25 dataset steps ahead, a median 40 px (p90 66 px) by our measurement, and calls TwoRoom LeWM's weakest environment. The v1 target was 154 px away through the door and the planner wandered off on CPU. Closed-loop CPU checks of the unconstrained planner: 4/4 successes at 30 px, 4/8 at 45 px, 2/8 at 60 px; failures drift to the wall, the door or a corner.",
      "changes": "start and target 50 px apart in the right room away from the door; budget 50 steps and 10 CEM iterations as in the LeWM TwoRoom evaluation; replanning every block (closed loop) kept because open-loop execution failed more often on CPU."
    }
  },
